  "last_message": "I added the retries to `capture()` in `larder/capture.py`. When the gateway raises `GatewayTimeout`, it tries again, up to 3 attempts in all, and if the third attempt also times out that timeout goes to the caller. All 4 tests pass (`python3 -m pytest -q`), including two new ones.\n\n**All attempts use the same idempotency key.** The original code made a new key on every call. If I'd simply wrapped that in a loop, each retry would have sent a new key. `docs/features/payments.md` says that is exactly what charged 41 members twice in 2024: the gateway can report a timeout after it has already charged the card, and it charges again for a new key. So the key is now created once per capture and reused on every attempt.\n\nOther changes:\n- **Tests** (`tests/test_capture.py`): one test has two timeouts followed by a success, and checks that there were 3 calls, all with the same key. The other has three timeouts and checks that `GatewayTimeout` is raised after exactly 3 calls.\n- **Docs**: I added the 3-attempt limit to the \"Retries\" section of `docs/features/payments.md`, because that page holds the retry rules.\n\nRetries happen immediately, with no wait between attempts. If the gateway's timeouts tend to come in bursts, a short backoff might be worth adding.",
